---
// Section divider, DESIGN.md section 4: an error-bar bracket, not a plain hr.
// A 1px rule with 8px end caps at both ends.
//
// The rule draws left to right on a scroll timeline, and the far cap arrives
// as it lands, so the bracket reads as a measurement being taken rather than a
// line being decorated. Decorative, so it is hidden from assistive tech.
//
// This was an inline SVG until it turned out not to be drawing at all. The
// path was `M0.5 0.5 V8.5 M0.5 4.5 H100% M-0.5 0.5 V8.5`, and percentages are
// not valid in SVG path data: the parser rejects the `d` from `H100%` onward,
// so only the near cap ever rendered and every divider on the site was a
// lone 8px tick. Percentages are valid in the geometry attributes of <line>
// and friends, which is the trap, but never inside `d`.
//
// Three boxes and a scaleX do the same job with no parser to appease, and the
// draw is now the same device as the scroll progress bar and the education
// rail rather than a third technique.
---
<div class="divider" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="divider-cap"></span>
  <span class="divider-rule"></span>
  <span class="divider-cap divider-cap-end"></span>
</div>

<style>
  .divider {
    position: relative;
    height: 9px;
    margin-block: 4rem;
  }

  .divider-cap {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 1px;
    height: 9px;
    background-color: var(--color-grid);
  }

  .divider-cap-end {
    left: auto;
    right: 0;
  }

  .divider-rule {
    position: absolute;
    top: 4px;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 1px;
    background-color: var(--color-grid);
    transform-origin: 0 50%;
  }

  @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
    .divider-rule {
      transform: scaleX(0);
      animation: divider-draw linear both;
      animation-timeline: view();
      animation-range: cover 10% cover 45%;
    }

    /* The far cap lands as the rule reaches it. */
    .divider-cap-end {
      opacity: 0;
      animation: divider-cap-in linear both;
      animation-timeline: view();
      animation-range: cover 38% cover 48%;
    }

    @keyframes divider-draw {
      to { transform: scaleX(1); }
    }

    @keyframes divider-cap-in {
      to { opacity: 1; }
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .divider-rule,
    .divider-cap-end {
      transform: none !important;
      opacity: 1 !important;
      animation: none !important;
    }
  }
</style>
